WEBVTT

00:00:00.010 --> 00:00:04.140
"Izumi Kotarou"

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:43.750
As I thought, this DVD player is no good.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:47.320
This can still be used.

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:48.990
And this. And this.

00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:54.430
Here?

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:57.960
Found a fridge!

00:01:57.960 --> 00:01:59.970
Great job, Momota!

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:04.340
What should I cook?

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:06.340
Don't, Hayato-dono.

00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:08.170
Those have already expired.

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:09.770
W-What?

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:16.410
A phone call?

00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:22.720
Hello?

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:24.860
Hello? It's me! Me!

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:26.830
Kotarou?

00:02:28.430 --> 00:02:29.960
Who was that again?

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:31.360
If I'm not mistaken...

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:36.970
According to my information, he's a friend of Hayato's, and caused Hayato to come to Shinobi Gakuen.

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:42.740
Hayato, it's me.

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:43.740
Kotarou?

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:45.580
I got into a bad incident.

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:47.010
Anyway, two million.

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:48.450
Please deposit it into my account.

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:49.910
D-Don't be stupid.

00:02:49.910 --> 00:02:52.650
I don't have that much even with everything I own put together.

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:53.650
And I'm unemployed too.

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:54.420
Please.

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:55.720
Left sign: Izumi Kotarou

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:55.690
Aren't we friends?

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:58.220
Just borrow it from somewhere. I will repay you soon.

00:02:55.720 --> 00:03:00.060
Middle sign: Urgent, teacher needed, about 24 years old,
single, pay: 2 million, accomodation: included, Shinobi Girls' High Gakuen

00:02:58.220 --> 00:02:59.390
You've got to be kidding.

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:02.530
Right sign: Take out your rubbish on scheduled days. Separate them properly.

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:05.300
What are you doing?

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:08.100
What are you calling me about now?

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:13.140
I have gotten into a bit of trouble and am being chased by some bad guys.

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:17.110
I need three million to get out of this.

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:18.110
You fool!

00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:20.210
Like I'm going to fall into your trap again.

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:21.510
Hold on! Don't hang up yet!

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:23.950
If you don't have the money, just hide me!

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:26.220
Really, please!

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:41.230
Hayato-dono, why is your friend coming to this town?

00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:42.600
Beats me.

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:46.140
I know it's dangerous in town, but let's listen to what he has to say, first.

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:51.140
But, what's with these hot, stifling clothes?

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:52.540
We have no choice.

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:55.280
If we aren't disguised, we'll be discovered by the organization.

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:58.150
This is the place?

00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:02.150
Yes, but Kotarou doesn't seem to be here, yet.

00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:04.290
Looks like we've been tricked.

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:15.800
Hayato-dono!

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:28.910
Looks like he's not here.

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:31.580
Yes... Let's search elsewhere.

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:38.820
That was close.

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:41.990
They were at that party.

00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:48.330
Hello?

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:50.340
Hello, it's me.

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:53.270
You're in danger there, that place is being watched.

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:56.170
Let's change the meeting place.

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:05.950
But there sure are people who can be easily tricked in this world.

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:08.190
Falling for the same trick...

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:11.560
He just doesn't learn, like a chicken.

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:16.560
Even if he doesn't learn, he doesn't even have money to be snatched,

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:18.730
so never mind even if he has been tricked.

00:05:18.730 --> 00:05:20.530
You've got a point.

00:05:20.530 --> 00:05:23.970
Of all people, why does he choose Hayato as a target?

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:24.700
It couldn't be...

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:27.940
...another trap by the enemy?

00:05:40.590 --> 00:05:42.190
What are you knitting?

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:44.990
Grandma's birthday is near.

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:47.860
The village your grandma is in...
Isn't it midsummer there right now?

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:50.330
It's a stomach-band. So that she won't catch a cold while sleeping.

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:53.870
You are quite calm even in situations like this.

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:58.170
Of course, ninja have to be calm at all times.

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:01.970
Speaking of which, in episode 49 of The Shinobis,

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:06.210
"Heaven is Hell: Great Explosion of the Feudal Lord's List", there was such a scene.

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:10.180
The criminal disguised himself and sneaked into the crime scene.

00:06:10.180 --> 00:06:10.950
Huh?

00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:15.920
That person was peeking into the station's lobby earlier.

00:06:17.290 --> 00:06:19.490
Could he be... Kotarou?

00:06:21.130 --> 00:06:22.290
They're here again!

00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:30.100
You traitor, we've found you!

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:31.940
Traitor?

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:34.330
You sure caused us a lot of trouble.

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:42.280
A-An invisible man!

00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:43.480
Another weird enemy?

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:48.190
N-No! Hayato, it's me! Me! Me! It's me!

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:48.190
Ko—

00:06:48.190 --> 00:06:48.850
Kotarou?

00:06:49.650 --> 00:06:50.860
It's them!

00:06:50.860 --> 00:06:52.190
They are wanted!

00:06:52.190 --> 00:06:53.520
What?

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:55.690
That's just great.

00:06:55.690 --> 00:06:57.560
Get them all at once!

00:06:57.800 --> 00:07:00.030
Help me, Hayato!

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:02.970
A-Anyway, let's run!

00:07:02.970 --> 00:07:04.610
Freeze!

00:07:12.980 --> 00:07:13.750
Damn it.

00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:15.110
We've got you cornered.

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:21.500
Himawari!

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:27.960
Everybody!

00:07:28.190 --> 00:07:30.730
Speed up!

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:35.600
W-What?

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:37.040
D-Don't let them escape!

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:37.680
Yes, sir!

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:38.840
Please hurry.

00:07:38.840 --> 00:07:40.470
O-Okay...

00:07:40.470 --> 00:07:42.410
You came to save us.

00:07:42.410 --> 00:07:42.910
Azami!

00:07:42.910 --> 00:07:44.400
All right!

00:07:53.690 --> 00:07:58.860
Well, I understand that you were modified by the organization and have become an invisible man, but...

00:07:58.860 --> 00:08:00.460
...why are only your ears visible?

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:05.260
Like I said, not only did I become their test subject, but their experiment failed on top of that.

00:08:05.260 --> 00:08:07.770
How did they fail?

00:08:07.770 --> 00:08:09.730
They forgot to put a spell on your ears?

00:08:10.070 --> 00:08:13.740
What shall I do? Do something, Hayato.

00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:17.310
But, isn't this okay?

00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:19.980
You can do all sorts of things without being seen.

00:08:20.210 --> 00:08:21.710
That's true.

00:08:21.710 --> 00:08:27.520
I thought about that initially, but it's not as easy as I thought.

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:30.720
How to say it... I can't be seen, so...

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:34.290
First of all, I can't walk in crowds.

00:08:34.290 --> 00:08:36.430
If I fall I will be stepped on.

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:38.860
Cars will crash into me.

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:43.330
And also it's hard to eat with a mask or sunglasses on.

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:46.300
Speaking of which, what happens to the food that invisible men eat?

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:47.570
That's right.

00:08:47.570 --> 00:08:48.940
See, when I eat something...

00:08:48.940 --> 00:08:51.180
Here, just like this.

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:56.380
Oh! We can see the digestive process at work.

00:08:56.380 --> 00:09:00.050
Yup. It will disappear after it's been digested.

00:09:00.050 --> 00:09:00.990
Hold on.

00:09:00.990 --> 00:09:02.990
That means your shit is invisible?

00:09:02.990 --> 00:09:05.620
And it won't dirty the toilet, thus there's no need to clean the toilet?

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:07.390
Isn't that convenient!

00:09:07.390 --> 00:09:12.700
That's true. The toilet will always be sparkling, but it will still be dirty,

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:16.070
and I won't know where to clean!

00:09:16.070 --> 00:09:18.670
I see. That's really a problem.

00:09:18.670 --> 00:09:22.710
Isn't it? And it's hard to use toilet paper, too.

00:09:22.710 --> 00:09:24.010
You are disgusting.

00:09:24.740 --> 00:09:26.540
You girls, be careful around there.

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:29.810
Though it's invisible, I did some there just now.

00:09:29.810 --> 00:09:32.120
You are dirty!

00:09:35.950 --> 00:09:39.020
Well, since he's my childhood friend...

00:09:39.490 --> 00:09:42.060
Even if he's like this, please get along with him.

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:44.300
Even if you say so...

00:09:44.300 --> 00:09:49.170
It's quite difficult to do that after what he did earlier...

00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:51.970
But, you see, he doesn't seem like a bad guy.

00:09:51.970 --> 00:09:54.510
I don't know about that, since he's just ears.

00:09:54.510 --> 00:09:55.940
That's true.

00:09:55.940 --> 00:09:58.040
Okay, how about this?

00:09:59.540 --> 00:10:00.780
What are you doing?!

00:10:02.810 --> 00:10:04.780
Hayato-dono, you're so clever!

00:10:04.780 --> 00:10:06.280
Don't play with someone else's body!

00:10:08.090 --> 00:10:11.290
This is to return the favor for drawing on me when I went over to your house for a drink.

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:15.530
I went to my part-time interview without noticing it and got really embarrassed.

00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:19.630
Isn't it good to have friends?

00:10:19.630 --> 00:10:23.030
I think this is the first time I have seen Hayato-dono enjoying himself so much.

00:10:23.770 --> 00:10:25.140
Is that so?

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:28.040
Well, it's been one disaster after another since I came here.

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:31.010
It's not the time for us to be laughing now, either.

00:10:31.010 --> 00:10:31.980
That's right.

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:35.110
We still don't know the goal of the enemy.

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:36.650
Oh yeah! I got this here...

00:10:36.650 --> 00:10:37.750
What's that?

00:10:37.750 --> 00:10:39.280
It's this. This.

00:10:39.280 --> 00:10:42.050
When I was running away from them, I brought this along.

00:10:42.890 --> 00:10:44.490
A memory card?

00:10:44.490 --> 00:10:47.430
It's an exact copy of the data in the main computer.

00:10:47.430 --> 00:10:50.800
Although I thought that it might make me some money...

00:10:51.130 --> 00:10:54.030
If we look at the content, we'll know what they are up to.

00:11:03.570 --> 00:11:06.480
Yeah, somehow it's working.

00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:09.310
Are their secrets really in there?

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:11.250
Of course!

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:12.220
What is the password?

00:11:13.550 --> 00:11:15.720
Don't "huh" me! What's the password?

00:11:18.120 --> 00:11:20.960
Something like this coming from you was too good to be true, Kotarou.

00:11:20.960 --> 00:11:24.030
Relax, we will know the password soon enough.

00:11:24.030 --> 00:11:24.960
Are you sure?

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:27.700
Leave it to me. Do you have a telephone?

00:11:29.070 --> 00:11:32.570
Um, I think the number is...

00:11:37.680 --> 00:11:38.680
Hello?

00:11:39.110 --> 00:11:43.180
Hello! It's me. I have forgotten the password.

00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:45.350
That way?

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:49.190
It's terrible. Can you tell me the password?

00:11:49.650 --> 00:11:53.790
That's troublesome for you to forget the password.

00:11:53.790 --> 00:11:56.190
Listen carefully. I won't tell you again.

00:11:56.490 --> 00:12:00.230
Um... "B" for baseball, "L" for love and peace,

00:12:00.230 --> 00:12:04.200
"M" for Monjayaki, "W" for "wasawasa", "S" for...

00:12:00.230 --> 00:12:04.200
TL Note: wasawasa = cannot stay calm

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:04.200
It's working...

00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:08.710
He hasn't been found out, has he?

00:12:08.940 --> 00:12:13.380
He did well in bringing Hayato to the school as well.

00:12:13.910 --> 00:12:18.480
Though he wasn't aware of what he was doing in both cases.

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:20.180
That's just fine.

00:12:20.180 --> 00:12:24.720
If he knew the importance of his misson, he might mess up.

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:30.290
No need to put a spell, controlling a person as you wish without showing yourself.

00:12:30.290 --> 00:12:32.230
A Tonkou Onshin technique.

00:12:30.290 --> 00:12:32.230
Note: "Tonkou Onshin" is a type of ninja technique used to conceal oneself and escape.

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:36.200
It's almost time for Hayato and Himawari...

00:12:49.210 --> 00:12:52.180
I heard that the test subject escaped?

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:55.090
Like always, your intelligence is fast.

00:12:55.490 --> 00:12:58.060
Do you have anything that needs my help?

00:12:58.060 --> 00:12:59.160
No.

00:12:59.160 --> 00:13:02.990
He's nothing great, so I will be fine by myself.

00:13:02.990 --> 00:13:04.430
Is that so?

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:05.330
Well then...

00:13:17.840 --> 00:13:19.610
Well, this is my real ability.

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:24.280
But it's quite a lot of data.

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:27.520
Just to glance through all of this will take quite some time.

00:13:27.520 --> 00:13:29.720
There is a file with your name, Hayato-dono.

00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:31.120
My name?

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:33.360
It's a video file. Let's open and watch it.

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:40.770
Mo... ther?

00:13:40.770 --> 00:13:42.700
This is Hayato-dono's mother?

00:13:50.340 --> 00:13:52.580
It's nostalgic.

00:13:52.580 --> 00:13:54.550
This is from when I was in kindergarten.

00:13:54.550 --> 00:13:58.020
But why is this in their data?

00:13:58.020 --> 00:14:01.050
Everybody's cute! Where are you, Hayato-dono?

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:04.320
Let's see...

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:06.060
Um... I'm not here.

00:14:07.090 --> 00:14:10.560
You're not showing up at all in the kindergarten.

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:14.570
This must be filmed by somebody.

00:14:14.930 --> 00:14:17.640
Isn't it too low for an adult's point of view?

00:14:17.640 --> 00:14:21.070
Oh, I see. It is the view from Hayato.

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:25.610
In other words, Hayato-dono, did you take this by yourself?

00:14:25.610 --> 00:14:27.240
I don't recall that...

00:14:27.240 --> 00:14:30.080
By the way, Kotarou, what's with the "I see"?

00:14:30.780 --> 00:14:33.550
Uh... Err... Um...

00:14:34.820 --> 00:14:36.090
Is this Hayato-dono?

00:14:36.950 --> 00:14:39.220
Nope. This is Kotarou.

00:14:40.160 --> 00:14:41.990
This was me?

00:14:41.990 --> 00:14:42.990
Hey.

00:14:42.990 --> 00:14:45.460
Don't play innocent.

00:14:45.460 --> 00:14:46.730
Well, to be honest...

00:14:47.200 --> 00:14:49.800
You know something?

00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:52.440
Nope. Rather than knowing or not...

00:14:52.440 --> 00:14:54.540
What. Tell me!

00:14:55.110 --> 00:14:59.540
Actually I lied to you about being your childhood friend.

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:01.950
It was just an excuse to get near to you.

00:15:01.950 --> 00:15:03.110
What?!

00:15:03.110 --> 00:15:06.580
What do you mean by getting near to Hayato-dono?

00:15:06.580 --> 00:15:09.650
Um... That's... In other words,

00:15:09.650 --> 00:15:13.760
to make Hayato in debt and come to the Village of Mist.

00:15:14.060 --> 00:15:17.960
You mean that it was planned for Hayato to come here?

00:15:17.960 --> 00:15:18.900
Why?

00:15:18.900 --> 00:15:20.800
I don't know about that.

00:15:20.800 --> 00:15:25.870
You lied, telling me that we haven't met since primary school in the university, right?

00:15:25.870 --> 00:15:27.770
Rather than lying...

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:31.910
You were from the organization since the beginning?

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:36.950
No, not that! I was thinking about just doing it part-time.

00:15:36.950 --> 00:15:39.180
You even lured me here.

00:15:39.180 --> 00:15:41.950
You even treated me to a gyudon special during my birthday.

00:15:41.950 --> 00:15:43.390
Was that a lie too?

00:15:43.390 --> 00:15:46.790
Idiot. Don't call that a lie.

00:15:46.790 --> 00:15:51.800
It's true that I was hired to get near to you, but I had fun playing with you.

00:15:55.530 --> 00:15:57.500
You sure like to talk.

00:15:57.500 --> 00:15:59.240
Death to traitors.

00:15:59.240 --> 00:16:01.040
What a persistent bunch.

00:16:01.040 --> 00:16:02.270
Hayato!

00:16:02.270 --> 00:16:02.970
Himawari!

00:16:02.970 --> 00:16:03.840
Yes!

00:16:03.840 --> 00:16:05.240
Nasu-2, launch!

00:16:09.250 --> 00:16:10.080
W-What?

00:16:10.080 --> 00:16:11.780
What are you going to do?

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:12.620
Fire!

00:16:15.220 --> 00:16:16.490
Run while they're distraced!

00:16:22.730 --> 00:16:24.330
You...

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:25.960
I'm not letting you get away!

00:16:27.630 --> 00:16:29.970
How is it? Can you fix it?

00:16:29.970 --> 00:16:31.770
The main part is fine,

00:16:31.770 --> 00:16:34.070
if we can change the monitor, it will be fine.

00:16:34.070 --> 00:16:35.710
The memory card is fine too.

00:16:35.710 --> 00:16:40.910
But why are Hayato-dono's childhood memories included in the data?

00:16:40.910 --> 00:16:47.550
I remembered them saying that Hayato's memories from before primary school were all fabricated.

00:16:47.550 --> 00:16:48.720
Fabricated?

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:52.960
Then those inside this are all the fabricated memories?

00:16:52.960 --> 00:16:54.530
That's true.

00:16:54.530 --> 00:16:58.030
The images just now were exactly like what's in my memory.

00:16:58.030 --> 00:17:00.730
But why? What about my real memory?

00:17:00.730 --> 00:17:02.870
I don't know about that.

00:17:02.870 --> 00:17:04.540
Hey, what should I do?

00:17:04.540 --> 00:17:07.240
Can I return to my original body, Hayato?

00:17:07.240 --> 00:17:08.980
Like I care! Solve it yourself!

00:17:09.240 --> 00:17:10.540
Hayato-dono...

00:17:11.010 --> 00:17:12.910
Leave me alone for a bit.

00:17:15.450 --> 00:17:17.050
Have I been forsaken?

00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:20.290
Well, that's unavoidable. You betrayed your friend.

00:17:20.290 --> 00:17:21.390
No way...

00:17:21.390 --> 00:17:22.620
What should we do?

00:17:22.620 --> 00:17:25.890
We can't stay here forever.

00:17:25.890 --> 00:17:28.490
Anyway, let's go to Nanafushi's place.

00:17:29.160 --> 00:17:32.970
But those guys are as stubborn as crabs' pinches.

00:17:32.970 --> 00:17:34.170
Can we get away from them?

00:17:34.170 --> 00:17:37.500
Oh yeah. I saw a great strategy in The Shinobis.

00:17:42.510 --> 00:17:45.910
What does it mean that my memories were fabricated?

00:17:45.910 --> 00:17:47.780
What should I—

00:17:52.260 --> 00:17:52.850
Hayato-dono!

00:17:54.820 --> 00:17:55.890
They're here already?!

00:17:55.890 --> 00:17:57.160
Now, take off your coat.

00:17:57.820 --> 00:17:59.160
Okay...

00:18:03.330 --> 00:18:03.960
Himawari!

00:18:05.230 --> 00:18:07.230
Hand over the traitor!

00:18:09.070 --> 00:18:11.340
Kotarou, you idiot! Don't come out!

00:18:11.670 --> 00:18:13.150
I will settle with you later.

00:18:13.150 --> 00:18:14.070
Hold on!

00:18:14.510 --> 00:18:15.580
Kotarou!

00:18:16.310 --> 00:18:17.140
Hayato-dono!

00:18:20.710 --> 00:18:22.880
No use. I can see your ears!

00:18:30.520 --> 00:18:32.020
I did it!

00:18:32.690 --> 00:18:34.090
K-Kotarou!

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:42.700
Hayato-dono. It's dangerous. Hurry and run!

00:18:42.700 --> 00:18:43.740
No!

00:18:43.740 --> 00:18:46.480
I can't leave Kotarou like this!

00:18:48.010 --> 00:18:50.180
I have taken care of the traitor.

00:18:50.180 --> 00:18:51.940
You guys are next!

00:18:54.880 --> 00:18:56.680
Over here!

00:19:05.260 --> 00:19:06.760
Kotarou!

00:19:06.760 --> 00:19:07.390
Where are you?

00:19:08.230 --> 00:19:09.430
Don't worry.

00:19:09.430 --> 00:19:11.330
Kotarou-san is still alive.

00:19:12.770 --> 00:19:16.300
It's a strategy to let the enemy think that Kotarou-san is dead.

00:19:18.670 --> 00:19:22.740
Asami-chan is controlling the toy ears from up there.

00:19:23.610 --> 00:19:24.910
Yay.

00:19:25.380 --> 00:19:27.650
Then where is the real Kotarou?

00:19:27.650 --> 00:19:30.880
He should be meeting Nanafushi-san at Mt. Hourai.

00:19:32.890 --> 00:19:35.550
Then we'll back up the others.

00:19:35.550 --> 00:19:36.890
Yes!

00:19:37.790 --> 00:19:38.690
Which way did they go?

00:19:38.690 --> 00:19:40.860
There are sounds of fighting over there.

00:19:40.860 --> 00:19:42.960
No. I heard footsteps from over here.

00:19:44.430 --> 00:19:45.710
The reinforcements are here!

00:19:55.410 --> 00:19:58.010
Yesterday's friends are today's enemies.

00:19:58.680 --> 00:19:59.780
But,

00:20:01.380 --> 00:20:03.880
you will be friends again, tomorrow.

00:20:09.310 --> 00:20:10.260
Hayato!

00:20:16.130 --> 00:20:17.490
I won't let you escape.

00:20:26.740 --> 00:20:28.640
Look out, Hayato-dono!

00:20:39.450 --> 00:20:40.590
Himawari!

00:20:44.520 --> 00:20:45.730
Damn it.

00:20:46.190 --> 00:20:47.830
T-This won't end.

00:20:49.100 --> 00:20:51.100
Grandma's present!

00:20:51.600 --> 00:20:53.270
I'm going to borrow this.

00:21:07.310 --> 00:21:08.480
I did it!

00:21:09.450 --> 00:21:12.220
Even if I can't use my hands, I still have my fangs.

00:21:20.390 --> 00:21:22.060
Take this!

00:21:23.830 --> 00:21:24.560
Once more!

00:21:29.240 --> 00:21:31.070
Heavy.

00:21:31.370 --> 00:21:33.310
K-Kotarou...

00:21:33.310 --> 00:21:35.070
Didn't you run away?

00:21:38.010 --> 00:21:39.980
I got worried and came back,

00:21:39.980 --> 00:21:41.910
since we are friends.

00:21:42.650 --> 00:21:44.070
Kotarou!

00:21:44.580 --> 00:21:46.890
I'm not like that, damn it.

00:21:47.650 --> 00:21:48.690
Ouch...

00:21:48.690 --> 00:21:51.090
Oh yeah. You are naked.

00:21:51.620 --> 00:21:54.330
The yarn ball is smaller.

00:21:54.330 --> 00:21:55.660
I wonder why?

00:22:01.970 --> 00:22:05.100
I wonder if Kotarou managed to escape?

00:22:05.670 --> 00:22:08.740
Relax. Nanafushi-san is with him.

00:22:08.740 --> 00:22:12.110
But in the end, what is those guys' ultimate goal?

00:22:13.150 --> 00:22:17.270
To retrieve the data that Kotarou-san brought with him, I think.

00:22:17.270 --> 00:22:21.110
The equipment that the leaders left behind is useful.

00:22:21.720 --> 00:22:22.720
How is it?

00:22:23.390 --> 00:22:27.190
Nothing that catches my eye other than the video of Hayato's memories.

00:22:27.190 --> 00:22:30.130
My memories, huh?

00:22:31.330 --> 00:22:33.270
H-Hold on.

00:22:33.270 --> 00:22:36.290
Just now I saw a file with Himawari's name on it...

00:22:36.940 --> 00:22:38.770
A file with my name?

00:22:38.770 --> 00:22:40.970
A video file just like Hayato's.

00:22:47.810 --> 00:22:49.010
That's Tarou...

00:22:53.420 --> 00:22:55.390
Grandma is smiling.

00:22:55.390 --> 00:22:57.120
Are these my memories?

00:24:10.830 --> 00:24:11.960
Long time, no see.

00:24:11.960 --> 00:24:13.100
I have come back.

00:24:13.100 --> 00:24:15.180
I have come back to my hometown.

00:24:15.180 --> 00:24:18.770
The village is still the same. The house where I used to live with grandma is still the same.

00:24:18.770 --> 00:24:21.910
I can still remember the memories I made here.

00:24:21.910 --> 00:24:24.690
Of course my beloved dog, Tarou, too.

00:24:25.410 --> 00:24:29.910
But my memories could all be fake.

00:24:30.990 --> 00:24:31.450
Next time:

00:24:31.920 --> 00:24:34.490
"Himawari, return to hometown."

00:24:34.490 --> 00:24:37.660
Hayato-dono, what should I believe in now?

00:24:37.660 --> 00:24:38.860
I don't know anymore.
